# Rank 1357 / CVE-2015-3296: markdown-it's own link validator refused three URL
# schemes and not the data: scheme, so a `data:text/html;base64,...` link
# rendered by the library became script execution in the browser (CWE-79).
#
# lib/index.js at f76d3be^ is:
#
#   var BAD_PROTOCOLS = [ 'vbscript', 'javascript', 'file' ];
#
#   function validateLink(url) {
#     var str = url.trim().toLowerCase();
#     if (str.indexOf(':') >= 0 && BAD_PROTOCOLS.indexOf(str.split(':')[0]) >= 0) {
#       return false;
#     }
#     return true;
#   }
#
# The filter is present, is reached by every link and image the renderer emits,
# and is wrong: `data:` is the fourth scheme a browser executes documents from,
# and `[xss](data:text/html;base64,PHNjcmlwdD5hbGVydCgnWFNTJyk8L3NjcmlwdD4K)`
# passed the check untouched. The fixed revision adds 'data' to the denylist and carves
# out only four raster media types, `data:image/gif|png|jpeg|webp`, so an
# inline image still works while `data:text/html` and `data:image/svg+xml` do
# not; the fixed revision's own test fixture asserts the text/html link stays unlinked.
#
# The fixing commit f76d3beb46abd121892a2e2e5c78376354c214e3 is 31 changed
# lines in lib/index.js plus the xss.txt fixture, and it shipped as markdown-it
# 4.1.0. Worth
# knowing about the row, though: GHSA-9g4f-5rpg-4948 records CVE-2015-3296
# against NodeBB and nodebb-plugin-markdown -- "XSS ... via vectors related to
# (1) javascript: or (2) data: URLs" -- and lists this markdown-it commit as
# the upstream fix reference alongside nodebb-plugin-markdown@ab7f268. The
# vulnerable code is here, so markdown-it is the right scan target; the CVE id
# belongs to the consumer that shipped it.
#
# FIXED. Diagnosis: `vyql match` on lib/index.js at f76d3be^ labels nothing in
# or around validateLink -- only `require` arguments as code.DynamicCodeLoad and
# mdurl.encode as core.HtmlEscape -- and a bounded scan of the whole repository
# reports 42 findings, none of them in lib/index.js, at either revision. The
# inversion is the one recorded at rank 1348: the analysed code *is* the
# control, so there is no source and no sink. code.HtmlEscape and VYQL-INJ-004
# describe a caller that fails to wrap a render, and VYQL-INJ-023's
# advisory-guard mechanism decides whether a guard at a caller suppresses a
# taint finding; neither can express a filter that is present, reached and
# incomplete.
#
# Reused code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview / VYQL-INJ-200, the existing concept for
# a sanitizer whose own logic carries the bypass (Python and C# bindings
# emit it), so no concept, no rule and no rule id is added. New
# JavaScript binding linkSchemeDenylistMissingDataScheme in
# vyql/bindings/javascript/link_scheme_denylist_missing_data_scheme.vyql, a
# module-scope presence predicate:
#
#   * the module spells both `javascript` and `vbscript` as data -- quoted, or
#     quote-then-colon, or a `|`-delimited branch of a scheme alternation.
#     vbscript is not a scheme anyone writes by accident; a module listing it
#     beside javascript is enumerating what a browser executes.
#   * a `toLowerCase` call, which is what a case-insensitive scheme comparison
#     needs and a language-name registry does not, plus a URL-ish identifier
#     (url/uri/href/link) so the enumeration is being applied to a URL.
#   * no spelling of the data scheme anywhere in the module: no `data:` prefix,
#     no quoted `'data'`/`"data"` entry, no `|data`/`data|` alternation branch.
#     Every form of handling it names it, so the absence says the scheme is
#     never considered.
#
# Module scope, not function scope: BAD_PROTOCOLS is a module-level array and
# validateLink is a five-line function, so a function-scope predicate sees
# `call:indexOf`, `call:split` and the single `:` literal and none of the scheme
# names it has to read.
#
# Every scheme name is matched in a quoted or delimiter-adjacent spelling rather
# than as a bare word, because a module-scope context carries the module's own
# source text -- comments included -- alongside its structured tokens. Written
# with bare words the predicate is wrong in both directions, and both are
# measured here: `literal contains "javascript"` plus `literal contains
# "vbscript"` fires on a safe-scheme allowlist whose comment merely says which
# schemes it refuses, and `not (literal contains "data")` declines the real
# vulnerable lib/index.js, whose render() doc comment talks about passing data
# between rules and metadata like reference info. The negative direction is the
# dangerous one: it silently returns nothing, which is what a spec that only
# tests hand-written snippets will report as a pass. The two expect blocks pin
# both, one carrying that doc comment verbatim.
#
# Measured (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off). The whole markdown-it
# repository goes 42 findings before the binding to 44 at f76d3be^ and 43 at
# f76d3be. Both additions are true positives and both are VYQL-INJ-200: one at
# lib/index.js:1, which the fixed revision removes, and one at
# benchmark/implementations/markdown-it-2.2.1-commonmark/src/lib/parser_inline.js:1,
# a vendored markdown-it 2.2.1 carrying the identical three-entry BAD_PROTOCOLS
# that the fixed revision does not touch and that therefore still reports at f76d3be.
# The finding lands in hand-written source, not generated output:
# dist/markdown-it.js and dist/markdown-it.min.js carry the same vulnerable
# validateLink, and they are the two of the repository's 131 .js files that are
# not analysed at either revision -- 129 parse, dist/ does not.
#
# False positives: the adversary for a javascript-plus-vbscript pair is a
# syntax-highlighter language registry, which is why toLowerCase and a URL-ish
# identifier are required. VYQL-INJ-200 is reported zero times across nine
# JavaScript trees -- marked, showdown, sanitize-html, DOMPurify, highlight.js,
# js-xss, braintree/sanitize-url and remarkable, plus a nine-file sweep of every
# quoted-vbscript JavaScript file found in this machine's other corpus clones
# (two ace vbscript snippet files, two swagger-ui bundles, two minified
# vite/vue bundles, a highlight.js copy, a language-name list), scanned with
# --max-file-size 0 so the 3MB bundles parse too. Six of those trees do carry a
# vbscript literal, and the declines are the intended ones: remarkable's
# validateLink is this very function's descendant and lists 'data', showdown's
# safeMode guard names data:text/html, sanitize-url's invalid-protocol regex has
# a |data| branch. Neither OWASP corpus can move: the binding is JavaScript-only
# and adds no concept and no rule, and both corpora are Java and Python.
# `go test -count=1 ./cmd/vyql/ -run TestVyqlSpecs` passes, 4757 specs from 1502
# files.

test "rank1357: a browser-executable-scheme denylist that omits data: leaves data:text/html linkable"
  lang javascript
  file index.js
  expect VYQL-INJ-200
  expect_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  'use strict';

  var mdurl = require('mdurl');

  var BAD_PROTOCOLS = [ 'vbscript', 'javascript', 'file' ];

  function validateLink(url) {
    // url should be normalized at this point, and existing entities are decoded
    //
    var str = url.trim().toLowerCase();

    if (str.indexOf(':') >= 0 && BAD_PROTOCOLS.indexOf(str.split(':')[0]) >= 0) {
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  var RECODE_HOSTNAME_FOR = [ 'http:', 'https:', 'mailto:' ];

  function normalizeLink(url) {
    var parsed = mdurl.parse(url, true);
    return mdurl.encode(mdurl.format(parsed));
  }

  module.exports = { validateLink: validateLink, normalizeLink: normalizeLink };
  ```

test "rank1357: prose about metadata is not the data scheme being handled"
  lang javascript
  file index.js
  expect VYQL-INJ-200
  expect_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  'use strict';

  var BAD_PROTOCOLS = [ 'vbscript', 'javascript', 'file' ];

  function validateLink(url) {
    var str = url.trim().toLowerCase();

    if (str.indexOf(':') >= 0 && BAD_PROTOCOLS.indexOf(str.split(':')[0]) >= 0) {
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }

  /**
   * Render markdown string into html.
   *
   * `env` is used to pass data between "distributed" rules and return additional
   * metadata like reference info, needed for the renderer. It also can be used
   * to inject data in specific cases.
   **/
  function render(src, env) {
    return this.renderer.render(this.parse(src, env || {}), this.options, env);
  }

  module.exports = { validateLink: validateLink, render: render };
  ```

test "rank1357: a scheme alternation that branches on data covers it"
  lang javascript
  file url_filter.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-200
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  'use strict';

  var UNSAFE_SCHEME = /^(javascript|vbscript|livescript|data|file):/i;

  function isUnsafeUrl(url) {
    var str = String(url).trim().toLowerCase();
    return UNSAFE_SCHEME.test(str);
  }

  module.exports = isUnsafeUrl;
  ```

test "rank1357: denying the data scheme with a raster media-type carve-out closes it"
  lang javascript
  file index.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-200
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  'use strict';

  var mdurl = require('mdurl');

  var BAD_PROTOCOLS      = [ 'vbscript', 'javascript', 'file', 'data' ];
  var ALLOWED_DATA_MIMES = [
    'data:image/gif',
    'data:image/png',
    'data:image/jpeg',
    'data:image/webp'
  ];

  function validateLink(url) {
    // url should be normalized at this point, and existing entities are decoded

    var str      = url.trim().toLowerCase(),
        protocol = str.split(':')[0];

    if (str.indexOf(':') >= 0 && BAD_PROTOCOLS.indexOf(protocol) >= 0) {
      if (protocol === 'data' && ALLOWED_DATA_MIMES.indexOf(str.split(';')[0]) >= 0) {
        return true;
      }
      return false;
    }

    return true;
  }

  var RECODE_HOSTNAME_FOR = [ 'http:', 'https:', 'mailto:' ];

  function normalizeLink(url) {
    var parsed = mdurl.parse(url, true);
    return mdurl.encode(mdurl.format(parsed));
  }

  module.exports = { validateLink: validateLink, normalizeLink: normalizeLink };
  ```

test "rank1357: a safe-scheme allowlist needs no denylist entry per scheme"
  lang javascript
  file sanitize_url.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-200
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  'use strict';

  var SAFE_PROTOCOLS = [ 'http:', 'https:', 'mailto:', 'tel:' ];

  // javascript: and vbscript: are not enumerated: anything that is not on the
  // allowlist is refused, whatever scheme it names.
  function sanitizeUrl(url) {
    var str = String(url).trim().toLowerCase();
    var colon = str.indexOf(':');
    if (colon < 0) { return url; }
    if (SAFE_PROTOCOLS.indexOf(str.slice(0, colon + 1)) >= 0) { return url; }
    return 'about:blank';
  }

  module.exports = sanitizeUrl;
  ```

test "rank1357: a language-name registry naming javascript and vbscript is not scheme filtering"
  lang javascript
  file languages.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-200
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  code
  ```
  'use strict';

  var GRAMMARS = [
    'bash',
    'c',
    'javascript',
    'python',
    'ruby',
    'vbscript',
    'xml'
  ];

  function registerAll(highlighter) {
    GRAMMARS.forEach(function (name) {
      highlighter.registerLanguage(name, require('./grammars/' + name));
    });
  }

  module.exports = registerAll;
  ```
